# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Everything except the TC dual-VLM tier works without any key at all:
# normalization, classification, MRZ, PDF417, the OCR label tier, the constraint
# engine, routing, the UI, and the entire unit-test suite.
#
# Without a key the pipeline still returns a valid response for every document —
# it reports MODEL_UNAVAILABLE and abstains to REVIEW on the documents that would
# have escalated to the VLM, rather than failing the request.

# Required only for the TC tier (Hunter/Mapper dual call) and for a full `npm run eval`.
# Get one from https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Where tesseract.js caches its ~5 MB language model.
# Defaults to the OS temp directory, which is correct locally and on serverless
# (the repo root is read-only in most deployment targets, and the default would
# otherwise drop eng.traineddata there).
# TESSERACT_CACHE_PATH=

# Optional (docs/DECISIONS.md §9). If set, every non-REJECTED /api/extract response POSTs
# its crm_payload here — bounded by a 3s timeout, never blocking or failing the request.
# Left unset, crm_payload is still returned in the response body for inspection; nothing
# is sent, and crm_delivery reports "not_configured".
#
# For a local end-to-end test, point this at the bundled mock receiver:
#   CRM_WEBHOOK_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/mock-crm-webhook
# CRM_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional overrides for the CRM object/property naming convention. Defaults model
# HubSpot's properties-plus-associations object shape (src/pipeline/crm.ts).
# CRM_OBJECT_TYPE=
# CRM_ASSOCIATION_OBJECT_TYPE=
# CRM_ASSOCIATION_TYPE=
